## Design & documentation (aims)

This project uses **aims**: design is the goal, and the durable design knowledge lives in a **capsa**
capsule at `.capsa/` — one record per fact, placed in the tree at the node it governs (placement is
scope). Work the design through the `/aims-*` commands.

- **Where design knowledge goes:** a boundary/ownership/architecture decision → `.capsa/decisions/`
  (append-only ADRs; supersede, never rewrite); a requirement/rule → `.capsa/requirements/`; the
  structure of a part → `.capsa/components/<slug>/component.md`; an engineering lesson →
  `.capsa/insights/`.
- **Anchor every record on filing** with `python3 .aims/aims_anchor.py` — `anchors:` for a record about
  file content, `--shape` for one about structure. Never hash by hand.
- **Read by placement:** at a node, read the normative records on the walk to the capsule root plus
  in-scope insights — not the whole capsule. If the read-time hook flags a record as possibly stale,
  re-verify it against the current code before relying on it.

